Regarding double spacing, it can't be ignored, even if theses are
universally single-spaced because there are large numbers of
undergraduates using LaTeX for writing papers and _they_ need
double spacing and will forever.

Regarding typewriter-like output, I have a set of cmpica fonts
(text only right now) which handle converting at the typeface
level TeX input to typewriter output (e.g., `` and '' go to ",
--- goes to --, -- to -, etc.) If there's sufficient interest, I
suppose I could convert math as well, but that doesn't seem as
important. The fonts are publicly available and if it was desired
to incorporate them into the LaTeX distribution, I will finally
get around to generating some much needed modified versions.

-dh


